  "independence_basis": "asserted by the dispatch of this assessment: fresh builds (replay/bin-rNN, removed after use) and fresh runs from seven frozen cards (card-r01..r07, distinct receipts) by agents other than the original executor, same host class, same instrument source (sha256 pinned in every card and receipt-bound). The receipts carry no executor identity, so this script cannot verify who ran them.",
  "scalars_verified": true,
  "scalars_scope": "Two parts. (A) Existing replay-certificate.json, unchanged: Sample, not the full original set. Replayed: selftest; b=16 and b=17 curves 0,1,2,3; b=18 curves 0,1,2,3; b=19 curves 0 and 3; b=20 curves 0 and 3 (r2 only, no aa was recorded at b=20). Every recorded arm of every replayed record is gated and independently compared: 30 replayed jsonl files (24 at b=16..18, 4 at b=19, 2 at b=20) against their recorded raw/ files. Dropped (replay/PLAN.md, 'Estimate, what was dropped, and why'): b=19 curves 1 and 2 (arms and size already covered by curves 0 and 3; CPU budget of about 45 CPU-min on a shared 4-vCPU host); b=20 curves 1 and 2 (their IC arms are already reproduced by the matched-rho cards' continuity gate in the 15b binary, raw/matched/gate-c1-*.txt and gate-c2-*.txt, each GATE OK cells=1; that is the 15b binary, not the original instrument, so it is cited here as context and is not part of this certificate's runs). Nothing dropped at the arm level. Smallest (b=16) and largest (b=20) sizes are both covered. Descriptive fields (build_wall, la_wall, wall_stream, vmhwm_kb, stderr walls, command seconds, build logs) are not compared. (B) Matched rho replay, card r01 of matched-rho-cards (run 8): the rho arm of the b=20 matched run (cards m00 and m02) replayed with the 15b instrument (sha256 79a821504c5b7a4639470d8e04dfd35fc6ad1a91d34bacee466461f36811e991), --arms rho only: curve 0 walks 0 to 3 (4 walks) and curve 2 walks 0 to 2 (3 walks), 7 of the 64 recorded rho walks (4 curves x 16 walks; curves 1 and 3 and curve 0 walks 4 to 15 and curve 2 walks 3 to 15 are not replayed and stay unreplayed). The sample must be a prefix of each curve's walk sequence, not an arbitrary subset: in the 15b source the rho loop threads one generator through all walks (target 0 is the shared k, target i >= 1 is drawn from that generator, and each walk consumes it for its multipliers and restarts), so walk i depends on walks 0..i-1; --rho-targets K therefore reproduces exactly the first K walks. Target 0 (the shared IC k) is in both samples. Every compared field (per rho record: arm, target, k, k_true, correct, steps, counters, setup_counters, restarts, escapes, r, cost, cost_cl9, cost_per_step, rho_model_neg, steps_over_sqrt_ell, steps_over_model, native, gae; per curve: the instance fields, symmetry with strongest_rho_symmetry == negation, c_add, native_names, native_note) is exactly equal; exempt: wall_total, build_wall, vmhwm_kb, arms_run, matched_rho, IC results[]. The remaining 57 recorded rho walks are not reproduced, so the 16-walk mean rho cost of a curve rests on its replayed prefix plus unreplayed recorded walks; the IC arms of the matched cells are not replayed by part B (they are in part A only to the extent that the b=20 curve 0 recorded arms are replayed there with the original instrument).",
  "supersedes_nothing_note": "Combines, without modifying it, the existing certificate benchmarks/20261018-blindspots-genus3-la-exponent/replay-certificate.json (runs 1 to 7) with run 8.",
